1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,380
This is Guetteur, built by Alex Alvord, Cloud Lab Works, Team Drift, for the
Open C V AI Competition powered by A W S.

2
00:00:10,380 --> 00:00:18,165
It is a depth-vision agent that asks for more evidence before acting, and
produces claims you can check.

3
00:00:18,165 --> 00:00:20,760
This demonstration uses synthetic depth scenes.

4
00:00:21,760 --> 00:00:31,239
The deployed path is a browser dashboard, A P I Gateway, and an ARM sixty-four
Lambda running Open C V five.

5
00:00:31,239 --> 00:00:35,752
Open C V filters depth, extracts regions, and estimates motion.

6
00:00:35,752 --> 00:00:42,522
A deterministic planner can recheck a zone, pause it, compensate for drift, or
request approval.

7
00:00:42,522 --> 00:00:46,133
The next perception call depends on that evidence.

8
00:00:46,133 --> 00:00:52,452
NumPy and Open C V independently remeasure each claim against the same pinned
input.

9
00:00:52,452 --> 00:00:58,320
The approval selector here is a simulation, not an authenticated remote approval
service.

10
00:00:59,320 --> 00:01:02,835
Here is the live A W S dashboard.

11
00:01:02,835 --> 00:01:07,668
We select subtle item removed, the rule planner, and simulated approval.

12
00:01:07,668 --> 00:01:09,865
The single-frame evidence is ambiguous.

13
00:01:09,865 --> 00:01:13,820
Watch the decision trace: recheck zone requests seven frames.

14
00:01:13,820 --> 00:01:18,653
Integrating those frames gives the planner enough evidence to request approval.

15
00:01:18,653 --> 00:01:23,047
The trace records the evidence, the action, and the outcome.

16
00:01:23,047 --> 00:01:27,880
One approved alert leaves the demo, and both receipt checks pass.

17
00:01:28,880 --> 00:01:34,074
Now run the same scene and seed through the naive threshold baseline.

18
00:01:34,074 --> 00:01:37,104
It does not request the additional evidence.

19
00:01:37,104 --> 00:01:41,432
The result is a missed event and a failed task.

20
00:01:41,432 --> 00:01:48,790
This comparison tests whether the perception-decision loop changes the outcome,
rather than simply explaining a fixed result.

21
00:01:49,790 --> 00:01:55,016
Next, a shelf item is removed, but the simulated approval times out.

22
00:01:55,016 --> 00:01:57,629
Detection and publication are different outcomes.

23
00:01:57,629 --> 00:02:02,419
The system requests approval, records the timeout, and publishes no alert.

24
00:02:02,419 --> 00:02:09,823
The score measures detection requests against ground truth; it does not mean an
outward alert was sent.

25
00:02:09,823 --> 00:02:12,000
The alerts section shows none.

26
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:18,034
Back on the subtle-removal result, both estimators pass the original claim.

27
00:02:18,034 --> 00:02:21,696
Now we deliberately double the claimed depth change.

28
00:02:21,696 --> 00:02:25,357
The deployed verifier remeasures the pinned synthetic input.

29
00:02:25,357 --> 00:02:29,476
Both checks fail and the altered claim is rejected.

30
00:02:29,476 --> 00:02:33,137
Small changes within the documented tolerance can pass.

31
00:02:33,137 --> 00:02:40,460
And two estimators over one input cannot establish that the input itself depicts
the intended event.

32
00:02:41,460 --> 00:02:44,818
This is the failure case: subthreshold item removed.

33
00:02:44,818 --> 00:02:48,596
The change is below the detector's effective noise floor.

34
00:02:48,596 --> 00:02:53,214
The dashboard reports a missed event and labels the documented failure.

35
00:02:53,214 --> 00:03:00,770
We keep this miss in the results instead of turning it into a success with a
different definition.

36
00:03:01,770 --> 00:03:11,632
Across thirty-three synthetic development-set runs, the rule planner succeeds on
thirty, compared with twelve for the raw threshold baseline.

37
00:03:11,632 --> 00:03:18,899
Event precision is one point zero zero and recall is zero point eight six.

38
00:03:18,899 --> 00:03:26,685
The corrected tamper suite rejects twenty-four of twenty-four cases; the initial
twenty-three-of-twenty-four result remains documented.

39
00:03:26,685 --> 00:03:32,913
Separately, three physical depth-only takes have verified archive integrity and
clean shutdown.

40
00:03:32,913 --> 00:03:37,585
That is capture evidence, not measured real-world detection accuracy.

41
00:03:37,585 --> 00:03:46,409
The M I T repository includes pinned dependencies, tests, deployment
instructions, the technical report, and raw results.

42
00:03:46,409 --> 00:03:51,080
AI coding assistance and this synthetic narration are disclosed.
